[2] Proof readout
  Residue-terminal fibers are close but still mixed.
  Erdos-Turan bins alone change mixed fibers by -21 and max mixed by -26.
  Henselian unit-rule bins alone change mixed fibers by -27 and max mixed by -30.
  Zipping both changes mixed fibers by -27 and max mixed by -30.
  Adding the coarse q/unit-excess lane leaves 0 mixed route fibers; exact magnitude leaves 0.
  Interpretation: on this target fiber, the Henselian unit rule is
  already a route-pure convergence carrier, while Erdos-Turan bins explain
  most of the visible contraction before the p-adic unit rule finishes it.
  The next lemma should prove this unit-lift split familywise, then stress
  the same rule on the full HYP-2963 bank before replacing exact magnitude.

